cff-version: 1.2.6
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Geospatial-RAP: A spatial epidemiology tool for prevalence mapping and local cluster detection"
abstract: "Geospatial-RAP is an R/Shiny tool for spatial epidemiological analysis using area-based case and population data. It generates prevalence maps, supports single-week or multi-week time windows, and applies spatial autocorrelation methods to identify geographic patterns, local clusters, and spatial outliers. The tool produces map-based outputs and downloadable geospatial results to support descriptive surveillance, hotspot assessment, and local public health interpretation."
